  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Start Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - 'Great! Now that we have the initial EMBEDDING, it is time to build the core
    of the transformer model:


    The ATTENTION mechanism.'
  - ATTENTION is the mechanism which will learn the semantic relations between each
    token in the EMBEDDING and add that information to it.
  - "You might remember that our EMBEDDING already contains syntactic information.
    Syntactic information is the information about the token itself, what it is,
    and where in the sequence it is. Semantic information is about what each token
    means and conveys, and how its position impacts its relationship with the surrounding
    tokens in the EMBEDDING.\t"
  - To get this information, ATTENTION uses three different EMBEDDINGS based on the
    initial EMBEDDING which you created on the previous floor. These three embeddings
    are called the QUERY, KEY, and VALUE embeddings.
  - To make these embeddings, create duplicates of the initial embedding and use
    NEURAL NETWORKS to embed each of them in their own way. Before embedding, set
    each of the WEIGHTS AND BIASES to the corresponding embedding (query, key, and
    value respectively)
  - In addition, the ACTIVATION function should be set to ReLU. This makes it so
    any value that is below 0, will be treated as 0 within the nodes of the network.
    ACTIVATION functions add non-linearity to NEURAL NETWORKS, allowing them to handle
    more complex problems.
